WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.060
So this is something I didn't end up having
time for.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.060
Earlier this week.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.799
But I did want to get to it because it's a
preview of what we can expect next week in

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:12.660
the vice presidential debate between Kamala
Harris and Vice President Mike Pence.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.730
When the Trump tax story broke, we learned,
thanks to The New York Times, that Trump paid

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:25.039
no federal taxes in 10 of the last 15 years,
paid only 750 dollars total in federal taxes

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:27.220
in 2016 and in 2017.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.810
But we also learned about Donald Trump's debts.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.109
And we talked about these earlier in the week.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:35.070
Three hundred million dollars in loans that
come due during what would be Trump's second

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.300
presidential term if he gets one.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.990
Four hundred and twenty million dollars in
total debt.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.440
Likely one point one billion in total debt.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:49.890
If you include other debts and and with which
we outlined earlier in the week, Joe Biden's

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:55.520
vice presidential nominee, Kamala Harris,
California Democratic senator, went on MSNBC

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.600
is Lawrence O'Donnell program and pointed
out the real threat of Trump owing people

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.600
money.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.600
Take a look at this video clip.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:09.940
This is why the American people deserve to
have a full accounting of the financial interest,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.490
including the indebtedness of the president
of the United States.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.250
And I and I do share in that concern.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.440
Who does he owe the money to?

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.540
Tell us, who do you owe the money to?

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.741
We need to know that the American people have
a right to know that when the president of

00:01:23.741 --> 00:01:29.520
the United States acts, he acts with their
priorities in mind, not what his priorities

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.340
in mind, of course, later on.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.930
This was clarified, including in our segments
about it yesterday.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.190
Donald Trump's debts are a national security
risk.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.270
We talked about that.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:46.760
Now, Kamala Harris was slammed by some people
because we do know about some of Donald Trump's

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:52.950
debts and some of Donald Trump's debts are
to banks that are household names, Deutsche

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.780
Bank and others.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:00.060
Those publicly known and acknowledged debts
are not really the concerning ones.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.010
Those are often tied to a specific property
or a mortgage.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:07.170
And there's at least relative transparency
about them.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:12.569
The ones that are the big question marks are
the ones that are from the period 2006 to

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:13.940
2014.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.940
And that was a time when Donald Trump was
spending huge amounts of cash that he doesn't

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.350
tend to have, as we're learning.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:27.870
And he spent huge amounts of cash buying or
developing or improving properties.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.370
And for a long time, there's been a general
question about where the hell the cash came

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.370
from.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:38.690
And now with the bombshell New York Times
story, we only have more questions about where

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:43.000
did the cash come from, given how precarious
Donald Trump's financial position appears

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.890
to be based on the documents that The New
York Times obtained.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:51.770
When we find out and as we did previously,
when we know that Donald Trump paid two hundred

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:59.160
million dollars in cash to renovate that Turnberry
golf course in Scotland, where did 200 million

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.160
in cash come from?

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.660
Because it doesn't appear that Donald Trump
had it.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:07.530
And now there is even more skepticism about
it.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:12.770
Trump is claiming, hey, we just had 200 million
in cash sitting around, but it is extraordinarily

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.980
difficult to believe that's the case now.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:20.330
And indeed, people who know Donald Trump's
businesses and his finances have said there's

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:25.099
no way Trump had 200 million in cash, particularly
at that time.

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:29.840
You can check out Adam Davidson's work for
The New Yorker as one example of someone who

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.319
really understands the finances of Trump and
the Trump Organization.

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:41.140
And to be clear, we don't know that these
are particularly sketchy debts tied to Trump's

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.620
claim of having all this cash.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:49.879
We just know that at a sort of general level,
it's not believable that Trump had this cash

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:51.250
at the time.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.879
We don't know where the cash came from.

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:56.100
And we know that Trump owes a ton of money.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.930
So so it's it's all of those three things
put together.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:04.879
Now, beyond that, not all of Trump's Deutsche
Bank debts are created equal.

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:09.440
There are these Deutsche Bank debts that,
like I said, are tied to a specific mortgage,

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.959
to a specific property.

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:19.289
But at some point during that same period,
2006 to 2014, Donald Trump went in the direction

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:22.440
of private banking at Deutsche Bank.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:29.229
And at that point, the paper trail starts
to get shadier and shadowy here, and we just

00:04:29.229 --> 00:04:31.949
lack a lot of information about it.

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:34.499
So there's sort of a double bottom line here.

00:04:34.499 --> 00:04:35.740
Two different bottom lines.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:41.879
One bottom line is now with the revelations
of The New York Times bombshell tax story.

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:49.099
Are there even more questions about who Trump
owes money to, where he got outrageous amounts

00:04:49.099 --> 00:04:52.979
of cash that don't seem to fit his financial
situation during that period?

00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:55.229
Oh, six to 14 you.

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:56.229
Absolutely.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.240
Even more questions about it which raise even
more national.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:05.150
Curity questions in terms of a Trump who could
be could be manipulable or subject to coercion

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.089
because of the amount of money that he owes.

00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:08.089
Yes.

00:05:08.089 --> 00:05:12.369
The second bottom line is, is this going to
matter in terms of the 2020 election?

00:05:12.369 --> 00:05:17.990
I hate to say it, particularly with more time
now having passed since the Sun story.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.850
I think the answer is no.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:27.789
I do not think at this point in time that
Donald Trump is going to be hurt in any significant

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:31.099
way by The New York Times bombshell tax story.

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:39.530
And what's crazy about that is for years we've
been saying the suspicion is Trump pays no

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.729
or very little taxes.

00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:44.439
Trump's not as wealthy as he thinks, as he
claims to be.

00:05:44.439 --> 00:05:46.210
Trump owes a lot of people money.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.439
It was all proven true by The New York Times
bombshell story.

00:05:49.439 --> 00:05:54.339
And yet the people who care are mostly already
not voting for Donald Trump and the people

00:05:54.339 --> 00:05:57.430
who are voting for Donald Trump aren't going
to be influenced by it either way.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:01.699
So as much as it pains me to say it because
of what it says about the American voting

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:07.000
public at this point, and it says something
very, very bad and sad, I don't think that

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.189
the tax story is going to make a difference
if you disagree with me.

00:06:10.189 --> 00:06:12.039
I want to hear from you.

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:17.780
And again, as far as debates are concerned,
V.P. debate on Wednesday, Kamala Harris versus

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:24.719
Mike Pence, I predict there will be fewer
interruptions from Pence than what we saw

00:06:24.719 --> 00:06:26.690
from Donald Trump.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:32.879
And I expect Kamala Harris is going to absolutely
hammer on Mike Pence.

00:06:32.879 --> 00:06:38.800
I'm actually looking forward to it, not in
a car crash way, but in an actually we might

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.099
get some policy discussion sort of way.

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:42.369
That'll be next Wednesday.

00:06:42.369 --> 00:07:37.879
Hope you'll join me

00:07:37.879 --> 00:08:00.059
on YouTube, Twitter and Facebook.

